-- A record mismatch's text does not depend on the OTHER files of
-- the project. This module is imported by nothing; it only interns `zq`
-- before `zp`. `M.h` passes `{ zp = y, zq = y }` where `f` wants
-- `{ zp : Int, zq : String }`. `Unify.gather` merge-joins shared fields in
-- symbol-id order, and ids follow file order, so the first field unified
-- decides what the second fails against. `check M.beni` alone must not
-- say the argument is `{ zp : Int, zq : Int }` while with this file it says
-- `{ zp : String, zq : String }`. Expected: the single-file text, whatever
-- else is in the project (fields walked in name-text order, or the
-- mismatch rendered from the pre-unification types).
pub y =
    { zq = 1, zp = 2 }
